  "style": [
    "Address the user formally with “vy” (vykání), as Czech system software does.",
    "Buttons and menu items use the infinitive in sentence case, without a final full stop (e.g. “Vytvořit poznámku”, “Otevřít nastavení”).",
    "Czech declines nouns, but a placeholder's value can't be declined. Phrase sentences so a placeholder stays in the nominative (e.g. “Poznámka {title} byla smazána” or “Smazáno: {title}”).",
    "Counts need the plural forms one, few, many and other; use the correct form for each (1 poznámka, 2 poznámky, 5 poznámek).",
    "Use „ “ quotation marks.",
    "Keep placeholders such as {count} or {title} exactly as written, and reorder them freely to fit the target language's word order.",
    "Keep keyboard symbols and key names (⌘ ⌥ ⇧ ⌃ ↵ Esc Tab Enter Space) and shortcut letters unchanged.",
    "Keep the source's ellipsis “…” and the middle dot “·” as they are.",
    "Translate meaning, not words; prefer the wording established apps on this platform use (Finder, Notes, Obsidian, Notion, Linear)."
  ],
